<BaseLayout title="Privacy Notice" description="Privacy information for the Lowcountry Digital Works public website and approved business-contact channels.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container readable"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p><h1>Privacy Notice</h1><p class="lede">Lowcountry Digital Works keeps this public website deliberately simple and minimizes data collection, tracking, and browser storage.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container readable">
<h2>Who this notice covers</h2>
<p>This notice describes how Lowcountry Digital Works LLC, operating as Lowcountry Digital Works ("LDW," "we," "us"), handles information associated with lowcountrydigitalworks.com and approved business-contact or project-discovery channels linked from this website.</p>

<h2>Information you choose to provide</h2>
<p>You can browse the public website without creating an account. If you choose to contact LDW by email, phone, text, or an approved project-discovery form, we may receive information such as your name, organization or business name, email address, optional phone number, project or service selections, and ordinary business context you choose to provide.</p>
<p>Please do not submit passwords, MFA or recovery codes, API keys, private keys, payment-card information, protected health information, CUI or other government-restricted information, or confidential customer/client records through ordinary website, email, text, or discovery channels unless LDW has specifically provided an approved method for that information.</p>

<h2>Technical and security information</h2>
<p>Infrastructure used to deliver and protect the website may process limited request and security information such as IP address, browser or device information, requested pages, timestamps, and security-related signals. LDW uses Cloudflare for website delivery and security.</p>

<h2>Cookies, browser storage, and tracking</h2>
<p>The repository-controlled public site does not intentionally use advertising trackers, behavioral analytics, nonessential cookies, or local/session browser storage for tracking or advertising. Strictly necessary security technologies may be used by website infrastructure when needed to deliver or protect the service.</p>
<p>Because the site currently has no nonessential cookie purpose to consent to, LDW does not display a cookie banner merely for appearance. If a future feature introduces nonessential cookies, browser storage, advertising technology, behavioral tracking, or another consent-triggering purpose, LDW will review the data flow and applicable consent requirements before deployment.</p>

<h2>How we use information</h2>
<p>LDW may use information you provide to respond to your request, understand or scope potential work, administer an existing business relationship, maintain necessary business records, protect systems and users, and meet applicable legal, accounting, or contractual obligations.</p>

<h2>Service providers and sharing</h2>
<p>Categories of third parties that may receive or process information on LDW's behalf include service providers supporting website hosting and security, business communications, and approved project/client-operations workflows. If LDW later offers provider-hosted online payment, payment information will be entered through the approved provider's hosted experience rather than LDW website code.</p>
<p>LDW does not sell personal information for money and does not intentionally share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising. We may disclose information to service providers acting for LDW, when required by law, or when reasonably necessary to protect rights, security, or users.</p>

<h2>Do Not Track and cross-site collection</h2>
<p>The public website does not intentionally collect your browsing activity over time across third-party websites for behavioral advertising. Because that cross-site tracking is not part of the current website design, a browser “Do Not Track” signal does not change an advertising-tracking behavior that LDW does not perform. LDW does not intentionally permit third parties to use this site to collect personally identifiable information about your activities over time across different websites for behavioral advertising.</p>

<h2>Review, correction, and deletion requests</h2>
<p>You may contact LDW at <a href="mailto:eddie@lowcountrydigitalworks.com">eddie@lowcountrydigitalworks.com</a> to ask a reasonable question about personal information you provided or to request review, correction, or deletion. Requests are handled subject to applicable law and legitimate business, security, accounting, contractual, or recordkeeping requirements.</p>

<h2>Retention</h2>
<p>LDW keeps personal information only for as long as reasonably needed for the purpose for which it was collected, ordinary business recordkeeping, security, dispute resolution, or applicable legal, accounting, or contractual obligations. Different systems and records may have different retention periods.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>LDW uses reasonable technical and organizational safeguards appropriate to the information and service involved. No internet transmission, storage system, or security control can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>This website and LDW's services are intended for businesses and adults seeking business technology services. They are not directed to children under 13, and LDW does not knowingly use the public website to solicit personal information from children under 13.</p>

<h2>External services</h2>
<p>The website may link to services operated by other organizations. When you choose to use a third-party service, its own privacy terms and practices may apply.</p>

<h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
<p>LDW may update this notice when website features, service providers, business practices, or legal requirements materially change. The current version and last-updated date will be posted on this page. When appropriate, LDW may also provide direct notice through an existing business relationship.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this notice may be sent to <a href="mailto:eddie@lowcountrydigitalworks.com">eddie@lowcountrydigitalworks.com</a>.</p>

<p><em>Effective date: October 1, 2026. Last updated: October 1, 2026.</em></p>
</div></section>
